    "sha": "91e412fdcb44ceee7a9d743b599c90cac24605c6",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDkxZTQxMmZkY2I0NGNlZWU3YTlkNzQzYjU5OWM5MGNhYzI0NjA1YzY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-24T08:26:55Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-24T08:26:55Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(mcp): run a stdio generate on a worker thread and honour cancel\n\ncamcraft-cli mcp ran each generate on the session thread. A long\ngenerate blocked every other call, and the client had no cancel.\n\nThe stdio loop now reads input on its own thread. A generate is staged\non the session thread (StagedGeneration, #2257) and finished on a\nworker thread. Other calls (get_job, save_project) answer meanwhile.\nThe result lands through the History only if the operation and its\ncached path are unchanged; else the call is refused by name.\nnotifications/cancelled drops the running generate with no answer.\nA second generate and open_project are refused while one runs.\n\nThe run time of the generators stays open on the issue.\n\nRefs #3035\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
